Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP stats: every disk cache record counted by what shader preparation did with it (records for another dynamic state by flag, prepared / kept / not kept / failed, ms a pipeline), and predicted records made for another dynamic state left out (the lesson of Fritchii v5.4 and v5.5); folded into EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP, no new switch, off by default

Follow-up to 0480 (EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP). Upstream read: Frizti/Fritchii pre-releases
fritchii-v5.4 (oot-gather-fix 8ce6c1e0d4; the fix is 9ea66c8273 "vulkan: precompiled pipelines
recorded with a dynamic logic op build where it is static (AMD)", by Frizti, found with a log
from koriko) and fritchii-v5.5 (4012e5271e; bd59d18c6a "EDS2 and dynamic vertex input in the
tuned settings", d64f34764a "frame generation never runs", 4012e5271e NVIDIA cache size).
v5.4: on AMD's Windows driver their preparation skipped 116,373 of 120,461 Ocarina records as
"for another device": the shipped recipe was recorded on NVIDIA with a dynamic logic op, AMD has
none, so the keys never matched; v5.4 clears the logic operation in keys while logic op is off
and converts such records. v5.5: players with Extended Dynamic State at Disabled or EDS3 had
preparation skip almost everything (the recipe is EDS2); it sets EDS2 and dynamic vertex input
back once.

Does our preparation have the same skip problem on RADV? No. What was checked:
- Where our records come from: only this console's own cache (vulkan.bin, vulkan_mesh.bin),
  recorded by draws on this console; prep_predicted.bin is read but nothing writes it yet
  (vk_pipeline_cache.cpp:2820-2828, vk_pipeline_prep.h header comment). Nothing is shipped.
- Which key fields must match: the boot takes a record only when its key's dynamic state flags
  equal this device's (mask components, EDS1, EDS2, EDS2 logic op, EDS3 blend, EDS3 enables,
  color write enable, dynamic vertex input, provoking vertex; vk_pipeline_cache.cpp:1649-1680),
  and 0480 prepares only records the boot took (disk_pipelines, :1682, :2852). Records failing
  that check are dropped silently: no count anywhere, the v5.4 symptom.
- Logic op on this device: dynamic. has_extended_dynamic_state_2_logic_op comes from
  extendedDynamicState2LogicOp (vk_pipeline_cache.cpp:680-681, vulkan_device.h:843-844), which
  dyna_state=2 keeps (vulkan_device.cpp:706-712 removes only EDS3 at level 2) and RADV
  exposes: every record of the console's cache carries the EDS2 logic op flag (below).
  With it, the logic operation never enters the key (fixed_pipeline_state.cpp:264-266) and the
  enable is static (:408-409, no EDS3 at level 2): our keys look like Fritchii's NVIDIA keys, and
  are made and matched on the same device.
- EDS level: dyna_state defaults to EDS2 off Android/Apple (settings.h:699-708) and dynamic vertex
  input to on (:718-724); the only overrides are EDEN_DEV_SETTINGS dyna_state=N and
  vertex_input_dynamic=off (headless/main.cpp:1032-1033, :1099-1102), which the play env does not
  set. The 9 Nov hand session log: "DynamicState setting value: 2", "Driver: radv 26.2.0",
  "Total Pipeline Count: 824", "1072 cached graphics pipelines are built when first needed".
- The console's own cache, read record by record (backup of 6 Nov, CACHE_VERSION 23, layout from
  the build's own headers): 1,597 graphics records (and 209 compute), every one recorded with
  EDS1, EDS2, EDS2 logic op, color write enable and dynamic vertex input, without EDS3 blend or
  enables, mask components 0, driver RADV 26.2.0, logic op 0 and its enable 0, no HLE macro, no
  vertex A, all vertex B + fragment. Two older backups (5 Nov, version 21, 819 and 860 records):
  the same. With this device's features 0 of 1,597 (0%) are for another dynamic state; v5.4's
  canonical rule (clear the operation while logic op is off) merges 0 keys.
So v5.4's conversion and v5.5's forced EDS2 change nothing here. What can skip silently on the
PS5 is a record written while EDEN_DEV_SETTINGS dyna_state= / vertex_input_dynamic=off,
EDEN_NX2_MASK_COMPONENTS=1 or EDEN_PE_STATIC_VERTEX_INPUT=1 was set in some test arm: the play
env's boot drops it without a count, and preparation never sees it. This diff makes that visible.

What changes (all inside PipelineCache::PrepareKept, which only runs with EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP=1):
- other_device(key): the boot's own check, as a bit per differing dynamic state (the host test
  below checks it equals the boot's check in every case).
- First pass: an own record the boot did not take is classified (task or mesh record of vulkan.bin,
  another dynamic state by flag, or no reason found) instead of skipped without a trace; known
  records are counted as kept or not keepable; a key read twice is counted.
- Predicted records (prep_predicted.bin, the planned next step) made for another dynamic state are
  left out ("another dynamic state" in the left-out list) instead of being prepared for a key no
  draw here makes. Folded into EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP, not a switch of its own: it only fixes the
  off-by-default path, and changes nothing until something writes that file.
- Log, after the existing "N pipelines known ..." line (which gains "another dynamic state N" in
  its left-out list):
  "Shader preparation stats: R records read (O own, P predicted): N not taken by the boot (a for
  another dynamic state, b task or mesh in vulkan.bin, c for no reason found), L left out, K kept
  already, U not keepable, S struck out, T to prepare, D read twice" (the buckets add up to R);
  "Shader preparation stats: M records for another dynamic state (own, predicted), never asked
  for here; recorded otherwise: EDS1 .., EDS2 .., EDS2 logic op .., EDS3 blend .., EDS3 enables
  .., color write enable .., dynamic vertex input .., mask components .., provoking vertex ..;
  this device: EDS1 1, EDS2 1, EDS2 logic op 1, EDS3 blend 0, ..." (as Fritchii's "Precompiled
  pipelines for another device: 116373 (EDS2 logic op: 116373 recorded dynamic, 0 dynamic here)");
  and at the end of preparation "Shader preparation stats: N prepared: K kept, U built but not
  kept, F failed; L left for the next start; X ms a pipeline on W workers" (wall clock of the
  build pass, for the whole-game estimate). K is read back from the store after each job:
  KeptStore::Add returns nothing and can refuse (a failed write ends keeping for the session),
  so a refusal counts as "built but not kept", never as kept. X ends when the last job does
  (the index commit and compaction after it are not in it). W is the builder pool's count
  (1 where parallel builds are broken), taken once with max_in_flight: GetTotalPipelineWorkers
  logs "Pipeline builders" at each call when EDEN_NX2_PIPELINE_WORKERS is set (play env).

Unset (EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP not "1"): T84, byte for byte in behaviour: PrepareKept is called only
when prep is on (vk_pipeline_cache.cpp:1747-1748), and every line of this diff is inside it (checked).
With the switch on, what is prepared and kept is the same as 0480 for own records; only predicted
records for another dynamic state change (left out), and no file of those exists yet.

Risks: low. Extra work per boot with prep on: a few integer compares for each own record the boot
did not take (0 on the 6 Nov cache) and three more log lines. The classifier is a second copy of
the boot's check: a later patch that changes load_graphics' test must change other_device too,
or the stats call records "another dynamic state" (or "no reason found") wrongly; preparation
itself does not depend on it for own records. "No reason found" > 0 means the boot's reader
(headless shader_cache_reader.inc) and preparation's reader saw different records.

Not ported, and why:
- 9ea66c8273 CanonicalizeKeyState (logic op cleared while off): no-op here, the operation is never
  in our keys with a dynamic logic op; our tree has no canonical keys (#895 not ported).
- 9ea66c8273 RecordedKeyForThisDevice conversion (recorded dynamic, static here): no foreign
  records exist; ours are recorded on this device. Not in our tree.
- 9ea66c8273 EDEN_NX2_NO_DYNAMIC_LOGIC_OP: only tests that conversion.
- bd59d18c6a EDS2 and dynamic vertex input set once: already the PS5's values, set by default
  each start; there is no per-user config with a stale value. If the stats ever show many records
  for another dynamic state, the port to make is a conversion of records recorded with less
  dynamic state than this device (clear what is dynamic here), not a forced setting.
- d64f34764a frame generation: a stale Qt per-game value upstream; headless sets frame_gen from
  its own video config and framegen.txt at every start (headless/main.cpp:1182-1189). Unrelated
  to shader preparation.
- 4012e5271e NVIDIA shader cache size: NVIDIA only; the RADV counterpart
  (MESA_SHADER_CACHE_MAX_SIZE, 1 GB by default) is far above ~13 MB for our ~1,900 pipelines.
- Driver rekey of records from an older driver (Fritchii's RecordedKeyForThisDevice, before
  v5.4): 0 of 1,597 records are from another driver today. After the build's next Mesa update
  every own record is "another driver" in 0480's left-out list and nothing is prepared until
  draws record them again; that line shows when this port is needed.

Expected effect: none on fps and none on what is prepared from today's cache (0 of 1,597 records
lost to a device mismatch: v5.4's gain, 4k -> 120k prepared on AMD, has no counterpart here).
0480's own effect stands: about 1,072 own records left to prepare at the first boot with the
switch (1,896 the 9 Nov boot took, 824 of them built at boot), so the walk's "on disk" builds
(554 of 1,387 runtime builds, 21.0 s on the GPU thread in the 12 minute 9 Nov session; about
15 ms each) should cost about 1 ms each. The stats give the numbers to check that: records for
another dynamic state (expected 0), to prepare (about 1,072 on the first boot, near 0 after),
prepared kept vs not kept vs failed, and ms a pipeline (expected 3 to 6 ms warm on 8 workers).

Test arm: no arm of its own; the lines come with every EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP=1 run of the shader
preparation test plan. Read them in A1 (EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP=1 EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP_FAST=0, first
boot) and A2 (second boot), then B1/B2 (cold, EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP=1):
- "not taken by the boot": 0 expected; any "for another dynamic state" with this device's line
  shows which setting wrote them. "no reason found" > 0: report.
- A1 "to prepare" about 1,072 and the end line's "kept" close to it; "built but not kept" =
  layer emulation / mesh as compute / no memory / the store refused (then a "keeping stops"
  warning is in the log); "failed" > 0: report with the log.
- A1 "ms a pipeline" for the whole-game estimate (warm driver cache).
- A2: "to prepare" near 0, "kept already" about 1,900.
- A0 (switch unset): no "Shader preparation" line at all, as before.

Checks (VM scratch /tmp/sp54-chk-6m2q; fv54/fv54_checks.sh, fv54_extract.py, fv54_inject.py,
fv54_test.cpp in the ports folder; log fritchii-v54-shader-prep.checks.log): git apply --check on
the T84 tree, patch and reverse dry run; every changed line is inside PrepareKept, whose only call
is under `if (prep && ...)`; no new switch name, no getenv or PeSwitch added;
prepare-vulkan-port.py anchor skips the same before and after (6), only vk_pipeline_cache_cost.cpp
changes, by exactly the diff's lines, and the baseline copy equals the build's; -fsyntax-only with
the build's flags (compile_commands.json) rc=0 on the generated vk_pipeline_cache_cost.cpp before
and after and on vk_pipeline_prep.cpp; no new warning with the build's flags (control: a planted
unused comparison is reported) nor with -Wshadow-all -Wunused-variable added; 16 injected errors
in the new code all reported, no other error. Host test (the classifier and the boot's own check
cut from the patched source, built with host clang against the tree's headers): 12,582,912 cases
(every combination of 9 device features, the 2 switches the check reads and 11 key flags, on 3
real keys), 0 mismatches. The 1,597 real keys of the 6 Nov cache: 0 for another dynamic state with
this console's features; all 1,597, each under the right reason, with dyna_state=3, =1 or =0, a
static logic op (v5.4's AMD case), vertex_input_dynamic=off or EDEN_NX2_MASK_COMPONENTS=1. The
cache was read with fv54/cache_scan.py, its layout from fv54/probe.cpp compiled to assembly with
the build's flags (key 1056 bytes, state at 48, as the PS5 build). Not checked: linking, a run.
Review (adversarial, VM scratch /tmp/fv54rev-k3x9; fv54-review/ in the ports folder): three
fixes in the stats only (K read back from the store; X over the build pass; W taken once),
all inside PrepareKept; every check above run again on this diff (18 injected errors, the
fixes' lines included, all reported), and it applies with lichii-1056 in either order (no
shared file, same generated copy).

